          "after": "Source-scoped proposal w04::I1201-BIO-P-catalase_c9322: #1201 isolated proposal: Add only the supplier-verified C9322 supplied form to the existing cas 9001-05-2 owner. Supplier COA names bovine-liver catalase, lyophilized powder,2,000-5,000 units/mg protein. The retained MeSHD002374 broad parent is species-neutral and #312 human NCITC61062 exclusion remains. Case 42 supplies the exact catalog binding. Case 48 establishes bovine catalase without that catalog; case 141 is generic enzyme reagent. Neither is silently identified with C9322. Existing non-name Properties aliases are not approved by this delta. Whole-owner publication review and inherited holds persist; uncatalogued case 48 and generic 141 cannot inherit C9322 form/activity. Raw source spellings are retained in case evidence and this source scope; no new globally resolving source-local alias is added. Full-owner publication approval and all source-specific holds remain pending.\n\nSource-scoped proposal w05::MATERIALS-C1193-catalase-source-form: Record the literal historical Sigma C-10 enzyme preparation as a supplied form on the existing Catalase owner. TOGO M109, carrying original_media_id JCM_M117, supplies literal Catalase (Sigma C--10),60mg and filtration context; the attempted direct JCM117 capture returned Nothing found; contemporary C100 evidence is not used to infer historical C-10 species, formulation or equivalence. Source-qualified proposal under issue1193. No ingredient roles, assay outcomes, complete-owner support or release admission are approved. Preserve all frozen source and owner holds; component uncertainty is stated separately from whole-material identity.\n\nAttribution correction only, recorded at https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1193#issuecomment-6718503816. Original wording remains in the immutable prior candidate/history trace. Historical catalog transcription, 60mg context, unknown species/formulation/C100 equivalence, all source hold