pplied forms; no unprocessed rumen-fluid equivalence is asserted.\", \"source\": \"https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/161\"}], \"mapping_quality\": \"FALLBACK_REGISTRY\", \"ontology_id\": \"kgmicrobe.ingredient:clarified_rumen_fluid\", \"ontology_label\": \"Clarified rumen fluid\", \"ontology_source\": \"kgmicrobe.ingredient\"}}\n\nCurrent scope: species-unspecified, variable clarified/processed ruminal material. The JCM and DSMZ preparation descriptions are distinct provenance, not identity-equivalent recipes or universal composition. Generic 'Rumen fluid, clarified' is a lexical counterpart of this scope. Both '(see below)' and '(see Medium No. 266)' tokens are source pointers: retained as REJECTED_LABEL with full context, not global identity aliases. MICRO0000520 cow-only identity and all old exact520/preparation evidence are explicitly superseded. MICRO0001898 applies specifically to DSMZ1310 and is not a substitute for generic/JCM material. The three coupled MicrobeDecoder parents only establish literal rumen fluid; their parts are separately ungrounded and no longer assert clarification. No guessed animal species, gas component or protocol equality. https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1204#issuecomment-6718503591",
