        "notes": {
          "after": "Source-scoped proposal w05::MATERIALS-C1193-polypeptone-boundary: Current BD Polypeptone is an equal-parts pancreatic-casein/peptic-animal-tissue digest blend. The old claim that Hipolypepton is a casein+soy blend is superseded by Wako manufacturer casein-only starting-material description. This does not assign bare MediaDive442 or Japanese Polypepton labels to BD211910; those product identities remain held. Correct the Polypeptone owner whole-identity boundary with its own registry identity and retire the three Hipolypepton resolving aliases using direct manufacturer evidence. Preserve other source labels and all ambiguous Japanese Polypepton and generic source442 provenance; no forced cross-brand equivalence. Source-qualified proposal under issue1193. No ingredient roles, assay outcomes, complete-owner support or release admission are approved. Preserve all frozen source and owner holds; component uncertainty is stated separately from whole-material identity.\n\nSource-scoped proposal w06::A-P-POLYPEPTONE-BOUNDARY:  Source-review correction: Hipolypepton aliases are REJECTED_LABEL because manufacturer distinguishes the unsuffixed casein hydrolysate from soy variants and from broader Polypeptone products. Original provenance remains in synonyms/history; no global product merge is authorized.",
          "before": null
        },
