          "before": "FOODON:03315720"
        },
        "notes": {
          "after": "Source-scoped proposal w05::MATERIALS-C1193-soy-peptone-boundary: Correct generic soy-peptone whole identity from the broader FOODON hydrolyzed-vegetable-protein identifier to a local material identity. Preserve source75 unspecified soy digest and all prior catalog/tombstone provenance; do not assign Difco Soytone, Bacto Soytone or Phytone formula to it. Existing branded alias claims require separate complete-owner reconciliation before export. Source-qualified proposal under issue1193. No ingredient roles, assay outcomes, complete-owner support or release admission are approved. Preserve all frozen source and owner holds; component uncertainty is stated separately from whole-material identity.\n\nSource-scoped proposal w08::op1201-soy-family-source-boundary: Primary product evidence identifies Soytone as an enzymatic soybean digest. Record that evidence and the exact scope of the four-member family on the active representative, without treating generic soy peptone, Soytone and every Phytone product as a reviewed exact identity. Three active owners share a broad vegetable-hydrolysate identifier; Bacto_Soytone remains rejected. MediaDive667 and MediaDive102 use Soytone and Bacto Soytone respectively. The Thermo/BD product evidence supports soybean-digest material, but does not allocate the shared 1089/833 occurrence totals to catalog products. Soy_Peptone, Soya_Pepton and Soya_Peptone were read in full, along with rejected Bacto_Soytone. Their existing identities, aliases, counts and holds are preserved; this is a bounded provenance proposal, not a completed family merge or product-equivalence approval. This note does not ratify inherited exact synonyms. The historical #260 reference is left verbatim as history; the live MIM issue260 is a hydration warning and is not used as soy-equivalence approval.\n\nCurrent coupled correction under https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1212#issuecomment-6718503130: 'Phytone peptone' and 'Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)' denote the distinct specific Phytone product now represented by MICRO:0001795; they are not exact names of this Soy_Peptone owner. 'Soytone (BD-Difco) or Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)' expresses product alternatives rather than one identity. All three original texts and sources remain unchanged as REJECTED_LABEL provenance. This is rejection of their identity claim on this owner, not rejection of the source facts. Other soy-product tokens, shared-ID occurrences, source holds and whole-owner review obligations remain unresolved where previously held. Original token objects: [{\"source\": \"manual\", \"synonym_text\": \"Phytone peptone\", \"synonym_type\": \"EXACT_SYNONYM\"}, {\"source\": \"manual\", \"synonym_text\": \"Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)\", \"synonym_type\": \"CATALOG_VARIANT\"}, {\"source\": \"manual\", \"synonym_text\": \"Soytone (BD-Difco) or Phytone peptone (BD-BBL)\", \"synonym_type\": \"CATALOG_VARIANT\"}]",
          "before": null
        },
