              "action": "ADDED_SYNONYMS",
              "changes": "VSO5.5H2O in TOGO M2262 is labelled vanadyl sulfate pentahydrate by the primary source. VOSO4 and VSO5 have the same elemental composition; .5H2O explicitly supplies five waters. ChEBI132758 exactly defines the pentahydrate, so this is a formula-ordering alias, not the variable hydrate or dihydrate. The source micromolar quantity remains contextual. Proposed only; integration requires content-bound full-payload mapping review.",
