      "issue_conclusions": {
        "rumen": {
          "body": "For clarified rumen fluid, the evidence supports withdrawing the cow-only exact MICRO:0000520 identity. Preserve the authentic record as an explicitly species-unspecified, variable processed-fluid local material, retaining separate source preparation descriptions. This scope does not assert equivalence of species, protocols or batch compositions. DSMZ sources permit cow or sheep; the cited JCM preparations do not specify species. MICRO:0001898 is specifically the DSMZ1310 preparation and cannot identify the generic/JCM owner. Supersede the W02 exact-520 support explicitly; retain original history as history.\n\nThe three incoming components in Casitone_Yeast_Extract_Rumen_Fluid, PY-glucose-rumen_Fluid and PYG_Rumen_Fluid require a distinct correction. Prior #204 comments already warn that their source labels say only rumen fluid. Redirecting their IDs to a local **clarified** owner keeps the unsupported processing assertion. The bounded correction is literal `component_name: rumen fluid`, `reference_scope: UNMAPPED`, no unsupported component_id, and preserved source-specific uncertainty/history. A generic UBERON grounding would require separate evidence review; it is not implicitly approved. This conclusion does not settle the separate sludge-fluid scope.\n\nSources: [MicrO0000520](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/micro/terms?obo_id=MICRO:0000520), [MicrO0001898](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/micro/terms?obo_id=MICRO:0001898), [DSMZ161](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/161), [DSMZ212](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/212), [JCM266](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266), [prior #204 conclusion](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/204#issuecomment-5208800239).\n\nIndependent full-owner scope review is recorded in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/existing-owner-scope-decisions-v1/`; decisions SHA256 `150af7315aa6688d4bc9adb3e2a27d0a0835ec8f8ac33d65b8951712b0382d81`, manife